                <pb facs="0206" n="177" sameAs="frus:frus1950-55Intel/pg177"/>

                <head>79. Memorandum From the Chairman of the Interdepartmental Committee on
                    Internal Security (Whearty)
                    to the National Security Council Representative on Internal Security (Coyne)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d79-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">NSC 68/17</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-07-23">July 23, 1951</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>ICIS Section of Internal Security Annex
                        for Report on Status and Timing of Current U.S. Programs for National
                        Security</item>
                </list>
                <p>In accordance with the memorandum for the Senior NSC Staff by the NSC Executive
                    Secretary, dated July 16, 1951,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d79-f2"/> attached hereto
                    is the ICIS Section of the Internal Security
                    Annex for the report on this subject. It is noted that the Executive Secretary
                    indicated that the initial drafts of the annexes should be available to the
                    drafting team <pb facs="0207" n="178" xml:id="pg178"/> not later than July 23,
                    1951. As you know, this report is to be prepared pursuant to the President’s
                    directive to the NSC with respect to the review
                    of the NSC 68 programs.</p>
                <closer><signed>Raymond P.
                    Whearty</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d79-a1.xml" xpointer="d79-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
